london_bus_TNA_56K.wmv","md5":"a1ecb3ad007c1243ce9bb902c067f330","mtime":"1227679778","size":"29104036","crc32":"96b7ed12","sha1":"11fb7523ca9a5543f0ca9cb2cd460dedeabfc983","length":"484.04","height":"304","width":"400"},{"name":"journey_by_a_london_bus_TNA_56K.wmv","source":"original","format":"Windows Media","md5":"3cb875c38d6c1225812d742b084cf6bf","mtime":"1129572750","size":"3023367","crc32":"6195b4fd","sha1":"2a20307bb7f3ea785002210c2586214b9b64ef6e","length":"485.3","height":"288","width":"352"},{"name":"journey_by_a_london_bus_TNA_56K_512kb.mp4","source":"derivative","format":"512Kb MPEG4","original":"journey_by_a_london_bus_TNA_56K.wmv","md5":"55b951fc6d2286282073a2b63c9766ed","mtime":"1227680076","size":"33168626","crc32":"66586983","sha1":"875d6801026baaf49ef4f877c4e07ade88e0ffde","length":"484.64","height":"240","width":"320"},{"name":"journey_by_a_london_bus_TNA_archive.torrent","source":"metadata","btih":"3547bc864e9e27b320ec7b1422107497a139e5e1","mtime":"1547527162","size":"33866","md5":"9e3ab5f81c465423b0c6cf0318b34a20","crc32":"1c4ed83d","sha1":"d39ff616642dc851e18c3f3cf381feda5bda8270","format":"Archive BitTorrent"},{"name":"journey_by_a_london_bus_TNA_files.xml","source":"metadata","format":"Metadata","md5":"f1addeb0e3e31893e9e8fda13828b25c","summation":"md5"},{"name":"journey_by_a_london_bus_TNA_meta.xml","source":"metadata","format":"Metadata","mtime":"1547527155","size":"1116","md5":"37a6d9b248f04ec71f37aaefa73b59ed","crc32":"7c971daf","sha1":"da93b6be10c3abc31e8a5b0b53a5278322b104d8"},{"name":"journey_by_a_london_bus_TNA_reviews.xml","source":"metadata","format":"Metadata","mtime":"1769676227","size":"6611","md5":"d47e71399bb394b1ed035cae05187a7a","crc32":"d3010878","sha1":"f80cb238dfad188a43c3e8f915f08ec48c0b8bc1"}],"files_count":68,"item_last_updated":1769676227,"item_size":786757229,"metadata":{"identifier":"journey_by_a_london_bus_TNA","title":"Journey by a London Bus","mediatype":"movies","collection":["british_gov_public_films","ephemera"],"subject":"London Buses","description":"An interesting take on London Buses intended for overseas distribution. London bus travel. Double-Decker bus.","date":"1950","hidden":"true","publicdate":"2005-10-07 10:40:29","addeddate":"2005-10-07 17:39:53","uploader":"florian@archive.org","sponsor":"Colonial Office","publisher":"Colonial Film Unit","sound":"sound","color":"color","runtime":"8:05","credits":"Public Information Films","rights":"UK Crown Copyright","language":"english","coverage":"Great Britain","updatedate":"2005-10-07 10:42:02","updater":"nVIR","backup_location":"ia903600_10","ia_orig__runtime":"8 Minutes 5 Seconds"},"reviews":[{"reviewbody":"There was famously one of these films that showed new-arrivals to Britain how to turn on an electric light. But maybe the British Government is holding back some of those really bad films? \n\nThis one isn't quite so patronising. Although,  produced by the 'Colonial Film Unit', the aim seems to be to 'educate' Africans on how to travel on a double decker bus. Indeed it features a journey by two African students. \n\nThe irony is, the script seems to have been written by someone who had never used public transport. Buses always arrive on time and the staff are always polite apparently! Or maybe things really were different in those days?\n\nWatch out for the 'cripple' who needs help boarding the bus! \n\nAlthough these days it seems rather anally-retentive and something of a sledgehammer to crack a walnut, this film does have a lot of charm and plenty of great shots of the old red Routemaster double-decker buses that are due to disappear from London streets in the last months of 2005. \n\nLater in the 1950's and 1960's many African and Carribean people would end up emigrating to Britain and working as conductors and drivers on the same double-deckers.","reviewtitle":"The Colonial Film Unit shows Africans how to use a bus","stars":"4","reviewer":"rgs_uk","createdate":"2005-10-12 10:27:41","reviewdate":"2005-10-12 10:27:41"},{"reviewbody":"Never mind the politically correct part. It is a great movie of the RT type of London bus. Despite what the previous reviewer said, the buses are not the Routemaster which did not enter service until some years after this movie ws made.","reviewtitle":"Interesting for a bus buff","stars":"5","reviewer":"R. Freedman","createdate":"2006-02-24 12:53:18","reviewdate":"2006-02-24 12:53:18"},{"reviewbody":"A great little film, well worth a watch.","reviewtitle":"london buses","reviewer":"wildwaylon","reviewdate":"2007-09-04 13:38:50","createdate":"2007-09-04 13:38:50","stars":"4"},{"reviewbody":"A cracking film!  I'm not sure that double deckers went that far out of town though!\n\nDon't get too uptight about any rascist condescension implicit in making a film about turning on a light switch. Public Information Films treated ALL watchers as untermenschen and dunderheads!  There is a lovely wartime film about how to make a cup of tea properly!!","reviewtitle":"buses","reviewer":"uncle nobby","reviewdate":"2007-09-20 19:07:16","createdate":"2007-09-20 19:07:16","stars":"4"},{"reviewbody":"Lovely and bizarre trip by a London Doubledecker that is \"always on time\", polite, and all sorts of other strange claims. I am not too sure why the Brits were almost standing on their heads to tell us that the busses are like the best thing that will ever happen to you, but here it is. Odd too that the film would go out of it's way to say how welcome black passengers are. Maybe this was made for black audiences in the US? A very odd odd film, and, I havent said this in a while, have I? HIGHLY RECCOMENDED!","reviewtitle":"You Are A Fool If You Don't Ride This Bus This Very Minute.","reviewer":"Spuzz","reviewdate":"2008-06-03 21:14:53","createdate":"2008-06-03 21:14:53","stars":"4"},{"reviewbody":"Just to give a bit of background, post-war Britain invited a lot of people from its colonies in the West Indies to come and live to the UK, due to a massive labour shortage. Apparently most black Britons can trace their heritage to parents or grandparents who came across the Atlantic during the 1950s.\n\nIt may be that these 1950s immigrants are who the film was aimed at, or perhaps it was aimed at a white audience, trying to help promote racial harmony. The white child happily playing with the black student does imply a sort of \"we're all the same under our skin\" message.\n\nIt's also worth noting that a lot of black immigrants found their first work on London's public transport system, as bus conductors, train guards etc. It's possible that this film was in some way meant to encourage potential immigrants to work for London Transport.\n\nRegarding double deckers going far into the countryside, yes they did on the Green Line, but they were painted green instead of red (which wouldn't be visible on this film).","reviewtitle":"Bit of background","reviewer":"kris1999","reviewdate":"2009-01-26 02:54:26","createdate":"2009-01-26 02:54:26","stars":"4"},{"reviewbody":"These are a totally viable method of transportation in and around London. I use them every time I come to visit. I love the <a href=\"http://www.busjunction.com\" rel=\"ugc nofollow\">bus to London</a>.","reviewtitle":"Nice","reviewer":"wooot","reviewdate":"2009-08-14 01:33:49","createdate":"2009-08-14 01:33:49","stars":"3"},{"reviewbody":"Obvious that the \"Africans enjoying a walk in the fields\" were spies.  The second one over the gate didn't close the top bar, meaning that herds of animals probably strayed on to the main road causing mayhem for the following 24 hours.  The bus was strangely full of too-eager-to please towny folk whilst in the middle of nowhere.  Very rum all round.","reviewtitle":"Highly suspicious","reviewer":"Rooftopjump","reviewdate":"2012-03-29 08:50:40","createdate":"2012-03-29 08:50:40","stars":"4"},{"reviewbody":"I always thought it was ridiculous how British buses had a conductor that collected fares. I hope they have modernized these days. ","reviewtitle":"Great historical film","reviewer":"Tim Crow","reviewer_itemname":"@tim_crow","reviewdate":"2018-04-08 01:12:31","createdate":"2018-04-08 01:12:31","stars":"5"}],"server":"dn600300.us.archive.org","simplelists":{"solo_manifest":{"solo_manifest_dn600300":{"sys_changed_by":{"source":"task","task_id":"5433296830"},"sys_last_changed":"2026-06-12 13:06:36.245614"}}},"solo":true,"uniq":527346433,"workable_servers":["dn600300.us.archive.org"]}